+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias at module level or in a class. The optional
+   description body can explain the alias. The directive does not create a
+   nested namespace, so aliases documented in a class do not contain other
+   object declarations.
+
+   The optional ``:canonical:`` option describes the type represented by the
+   alias. When supplied, it is shown after the alias name in the signature and
+   parsed as a type annotation, so referenced types are cross-referenced
+   normally. Without it, the alias is still indexed and can be cross-referenced.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      Describe the type represented by the alias.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the module containing the alias. The default value is the
+      module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
 .. rst:directive:: .. py:exception:: name
                    .. py:exception:: name(parameters)
                    .. py:exception:: name[type parameters](parameters)
